--TEST--
`ClassInfo::parent` walks a program's own error classes up to the built-in class they extend, and names each level as it is declared — `rule:core-classes/reflect`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::parent
// A program's error classes extend a built-in one. The walk names each of the
// program's own levels with its namespace, then the built-in classes above.
namespace Shop;

use RuntimeError;

class ShopError extends RuntimeError {}

class OrderError extends ShopError {}

final class OrderNotFound extends OrderError {}

?Core\Reflect\ClassInfo $level = Core\Reflect::forObject(new OrderNotFound("missing"));
int $depth = 0;
while ($level != null) {
    ?string $parent = $level->parent();
    echo $depth as string, " ", $level->name(), " -> ", $parent ?? "<null>", "\n";
    $level = $parent == null ? null : Core\Reflect::forClass($parent);
    $depth = $depth + 1;
}
--EXPECT--
0 Shop\OrderNotFound -> Shop\OrderError
1 Shop\OrderError -> Shop\ShopError
2 Shop\ShopError -> RuntimeError
3 RuntimeError -> Throwable
4 Throwable -> <null>
